    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1371">

                <pb facs="1632" n="1434" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Truman Papers</hi></note>
                <head>No. 1371<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President’s Chief of
                        Staff</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1371-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Potsdam</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-24">July 24 (?), 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Our attitude is<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1371-f2"/> free passage of ships of all
                    nations through the Straits on equal terms and there should be no fortifications
                    on the shores of the Straits[.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1371-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1371-f1-content">
                <p>From the fragmentary nature of this manuscript memorandum and its location in the
                        Truman Papers, it seems probable that
                        Leahy wrote it and passed it to
                        Truman during the course of the
                    discussion of the Straits at the Eighth Plenary Meeting, July 24. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg366">p. 366</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1371-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1371-f2-content">
                <p>Leahy originally wrote “should be”, but
                    changed this wording to “is”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
